  "summary_en": "Opinion article on the Indonesian Supreme Court's news site examining whether AI is a legal subject or object under Indonesian law. It concludes AI currently is an object, lacks the intent needed for criminal responsibility, and liability falls on AI creators and operators, while noting calls for clearer regulation.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Under Indonesian positive law AI is a legal object, treated as an electronic system or electronic agent under the ITE Law.",
   "AI could be analogised to a worker under the Civil Code, making owners liable as employers.",
   "AI lacks consciousness and intent, so criminal liability falls on its creator or user.",
   "GR 71/2019 places responsibility on the system operator.",
   "Clear legal norms on AI status and liability are needed."
